The region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062447/assets/5497f23e51d1e745fef1cf39d6c1a8ada22b25e8c9c7b87f5d5338e85a941739.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=y{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}x$ and $Q(x,y)=-{y}^{2}x+{y}^{4}.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2yx+{y}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2yx+4{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2yx+{y}^{3})+(-2yx+4{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}5{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343114 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343115 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343116 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343117 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343118 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1041 "selection" 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343114 13194139535310 true] [17592186343113 1110 #uuid "ed46141b-e20e-540b-9ec5-0fa9b3f0c51f" 13194139535310 true] [17592186343114 1034 "{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}5{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535310 true] [17592186343114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535310 true] [17592186343114 1111 #uuid "8cb8a4e1-3751-561c-8686-4a2d4f31fef4" 13194139535310 true] [17592186343115 1034 "{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}5{y}^{3}(x-5)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535310 true] [17592186343115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535310 true] [17592186343115 1111 #uuid "14fe9f41-9ece-51d5-af87-b